UPDATE companies SET description='AMBAC International, based in Elgin, South Carolina, traces its roots to 1910 when it began as American Bosch, manufacturing heavy-duty engine components in the United States. The company is employee-owned, operating under an open-book leadership model that shares financial transparency with its workforce.

The company specializes in precision machining, grinding, and honing, holding micron-level tolerances for low- to medium-volume production. Its services span manufacturing and remanufacturing of complex mechanical assemblies, including reverse engineering, product design, heat treatment, and assembly with test. Production volumes range from 100 to 50,000 estimated annual units, with a work envelope of 0.25 to 18 inches and diameters up to approximately 6 inches.

AMBAC serves aerospace, defense, and industrial original equipment manufacturers, as well as remanufacturing distributors. Its core focus is power and fluid components such as camshafts, valves, pumps, and injectors for high-pressure fluid flow and powertrain applications.

The firm differentiates itself through its century-long legacy, employee ownership culture, and relationship-based approach that emphasizes personalized service and technical depth in engineering and metallurgy.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision machining", "Grinding", "Honing", "Remanufacturing", "Complex assembly and test", "Reverse engineering", "Product design", "Design for manufacturing", "Industrialization", "Program management", "Engineering services", "Quality assurance", "Heat treating", "Supply chain management", "Metallurgical laboratory", "Measurement and inspection", "Engineering laboratory"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense", "Industrial OEMs", "Heavy-duty engine", "Power and fluid components", "Remanufacturing distribution"], "materials": ["Ferrous metals", "Nonferrous metals", "Stainless steel", "Alloys", "Forgings", "Castings", "Billet", "Bar stock"], "equipment": [], "volume": "100 to 50,000 EAU (Estimated Annual Usage)", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "Micron-level tolerances (\u00b5 tolerances)", "built_on": ["Employee-owned with open-book leadership", "Micron-level precision tolerances", "Production volumes from 100 to 50,000 EAU", "Century of manufacturing heritage since 1910", "In-house reverse engineering and product design"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1910 -> db, /about-us", "Headquarters Elgin, South Carolina -> db", "Employee-owned -> /about-us, /", "Formerly American Bosch -> /about-us", "Machining, grinding, honing specialization -> /, /services", "Micron-level tolerances -> /services, /about-us", "Production volumes 100 to 50,000 EAU -> /services", "Work envelope 0.25 to 18 inches, ~6 inch diameter -> /services", "Industries: aerospace, defense, industrial OEMs -> /", "Remanufacturing complex assemblies -> /", "Materials: Ferrous, Nonferrous, Stainless, Alloys, Forgings, Castings, Billet, Bar -> /services", "Capabilities: reverse engineering, product design, design for manufacturing, industrializ