UPDATE companies SET description='ATACO Steel Products Corporation, a privately owned manufacturer of metal stampings, has operated from Cedarburg, Wisconsin since its founding in 1946. The company began as a deep draw stamping specialist and has grown into a full-service metal fabrication partner.

The company produces deep drawn metal stampings up to 16 inches in depth of draw, alongside conventional metal stamping, 3D 5-axis laser cutting, 2D laser cutting and press brake fabrication, robotic and manual welding, and sheet metal engineering services including pre-design feasibility, design for manufacturability, and PFMEA. An in-house Cut & Etch Lab supports weld evaluation to AWS D1.1, ISO 3834, and AWS 14.3 standards. The facility houses coordinate measuring machines, laser scanning systems, and a range of hardness and functional gaging equipment.

ATACO serves original equipment manufacturers in agriculture, commercial food equipment, construction, lawn and garden, material handling, military, powersports, rail, and sustainability sectors. Customers include agricultural equipment builders, rail component suppliers, and construction machinery OEMs who rely on the shop for high-tonnage, close-tolerance stampings and fabricated assemblies such as tanks, reservoirs, and deep drawn shells.

The company emphasizes engineering collaboration, tooling-free laser trim and pierce operations, and an internal test lab that reduces third-party inspection lead times. Its fundamentals stress consistent quality, on-time delivery, and a culture of continuous improvement across its quality management system.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Deep draw metal stamping", "3D 5-axis laser cutting", "Metal stamping", "Metal fabrication (2D cutting)", "Sheet metal engineering", "Welding (robotic, pulse, resistance, MIG)", "Cut & etch lab", "Secondary forming and finishing", "Pre-design technical support", "Design for manufacturability", "PFMEA", "First article inspection", "Process capability studies", "CMM inspection", "2D/3D laser scanning", "Hardness testing", "Functional gaging"], "industries": ["Agriculture", "Commercial Food Equipment", "Construction", "Lawn & Garden", "Material Handling", "Military", "Powersports", "Rail", "Sustainability Products"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Brown & Sharpe XCEL 12-20-10 (DCC) Coordinate Measuring Machine", "Portage Measuring Machine (70\" x 100\" table)", "Amada FabriVISION Laser (2D scanning)", "Hexagon Metrology ROMER Arm (3D scanning)", "Brinell Hardness Tester", "Robotic welders", "Pulse welders", "Resistance welders", "MIG welding equipment (300\u2013450 amp)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Deep draw stamping expertise since 1946", "3D 5-axis laser cutting eliminates expensive tooling for trim and pierce operations", "In-house Cut & Etch Lab for AWS D1.1, ISO 3834, and AWS 14.3 weld compliance without third-party testing", "Engineering support including pre-design feasibility, design for manufacturability, and PFMEA", "Robotic, pulse, resistance, and MIG welding (300\u2013450 amp) capacity"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1946 -> db, /about", "Headquarters Cedarburg, Wisconsin -> db, /about", "Privately owned -> /about", "Capabilities: deep draw stam