UPDATE companies SET description='ATEX Technologies, Inc. was founded in 2006 in Pinebluff, North Carolina. The company was created to address the need for high-quality textiles exclusively for implantable medical devices, backed by an organization capable of meeting demanding regulatory and quality requirements.

The company engineers custom implantable medical textile components using knitting, weaving, braiding, and non-woven technologies. Its capabilities span yarn development, textile formation, finishing, testing, and validation — all performed in-house. ATEX works with materials such as PET (for which it holds an FDA Master File), polypropylene, ultra-high-molecular-weight polyethylene, liquid crystal polymer, and other thermoplastics.

ATEX serves medical device manufacturers across clinical specialties including vascular and structural heart, orthopedic and robotic surgery, general surgery, and neurology and regenerative medicine. Its components — sheets, rings, tubes, tapers, and complex 3D structures — are designed to integrate into customers'' devices, from fenestrated grafts and heart valve leaflets to medical scaffolds.

ATEX distinguishes itself as a medical textile solutions partner rather than a contract manufacturer, emphasizing engineering collaboration, innovation, and a relationship-first approach. The company cites four pillars — Technology, Innovation, Quality, and Character — and has invested in mistake-proofing systems to mitigate risk and ensure consistency throughout the product life cycle.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Knitting", "Weaving", "Braiding", "Non-woven fabrication", "Yarn development", "Textile formation", "Finishing", "Testing", "Validation", "Custom implantable textile components", "Biomedical textile engineering", "Material selection and development"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Vascular", "Structural heart", "Orthopedic", "Robotic surgery", "General surgery", "Neurology", "Regenerative medicine"], "materials": ["PET (FDA Master File)", "Polypropylene", "Ultra-high-molecular-weight polyethylene (UHMWPE)", "Liquid crystal polymer (LCP)", "Thermoplastics"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% focus on the medical device market", "Not a contract manufacturer but a medical textile solutions partner", "Yarn development, textile formation, finishing, testing, and validation all under one roof", "Mistake-proofing systems that mitigate risk and reduce errors", "Engineering and application expertise from concept through validation"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2006 in Pinebluff, NC -> db", "Specializes in implantable textiles and custom medical textile solutions for device manufacturers -> /", "Uses knitting, weaving, braiding, non-woven technologies -> / (FAQ)", "Offers yarn development, textile formation, finishing, testing, validation under one roof -> / (FAQ)", "Materials: PET (FDA Master File), Polypro, UHMWPE, LCP, thermoplastics -> / (FAQ)", "Clinical specialties: vascular/structural heart, orthopedic/robotic surgery, general surgery, neurology/regenerative medicine -> /",