UPDATE companies SET description='KYOCERA AVX, headquartered in Fountain Inn, South Carolina, traces its origins to 1922 when Radiola Wireless was established in New York City. Through a series of transformations—including the Aerovox era and the founding of Electrical Reactance Corp in Myrtle Beach, South Carolina—the company was formally incorporated as AVX Corporation in 1972. A 1990 merger with Japan’s Kyocera Corporation led to full ownership by Kyocera in 2020, and the business adopted the KYOCERA AVX brand in 2021.

The company designs and manufactures a broad portfolio of advanced electronic components, including capacitors, connectors, antennas, filters, crystal devices, sensing and control modules, diodes, varistors, fuses, inductors, couplers, thermal management solutions, thermistors, resistive products, and SAW devices. It operates several dozen research, development, and manufacturing facilities across more than 15 countries, supported by a global workforce of over 15,000 engineers, researchers, technicians, and specialists. Core capabilities include custom design services and laser direct structuring (LDS) manufacturing.

KYOCERA AVX serves customers in automotive, aerospace, medical, industrial, military and defense, consumer electronics, 5G and IoT, aviation, automation, renewables, and high-temperature applications. Its components are engineered for mission-critical systems ranging from automotive power supplies and satellite communications to medical implants and industrial sensors.

The company emphasizes a “zero defect” quality culture, continuous improvement of its quality management systems, and an employee-first philosophy that it credits for its collaborative innovation. Its stated mission is to innovate technologies and products for tomorrow’s solutions while delivering superior customer satisfaction.', certifications=ARRAY['MIL-SPEC']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom Design Services", "LDS (Laser Direct Structuring) Manufacturing Services", "Engineering Design Services", "Component Search and Selection Tools", "Circuit Simulation (SpiCAT)", "Antenna Integration Tools", "MIL-SPEC / DLA Qualified Manufacturing", "Multilayer Ceramic Capacitor Manufacturing", "Tantalum Capacitor Manufacturing", "Aluminum Electrolytic Capacitor Manufacturing", "Film Capacitor Manufacturing", "Connector Manufacturing", "Antenna Manufacturing", "RF/Microwave Filter Manufacturing", "SAW Device Manufacturing", "Crystal Device Manufacturing", "Sensing & Control Module Manufacturing", "Resistive Product Manufacturing", "Thermal Management Solutions", "Varistor Manufacturing", "Fuse Manufacturing", "Inductor Manufacturing", "Coupler Manufacturing", "Thin Film Passive Component Manufacturing"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Aerospace", "Medical", "Sensors", "Consumer", "Military / Defense", "Industrial", "5G / IoT", "Aviation", "Automation", "Renewables", "High Temperature"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Global footprint of several dozen R&D and manufacturing facilities across 15+ countries", "Workforce of over 15,000 engineers, researchers, and technical specialists", "Custom design services and laser direct structuring (LDS) manufacturing capabilities", "MIL-SPEC qualified components for military and defense programs", "Zero-defect quality culture with continuous improvement focus"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Fountain Inn, SC -> page ''/''", "Founded 1922 as Radiola Wireless -> pag