UPDATE companies SET description='Able Coil & Electronics was founded in 1969 in Bolton, Connecticut, by Ken Rockefeller to address a growing demand for high-quality coil winding and assembly services. The company remains under Rockefeller family leadership, with Steven Rockefeller serving as president since 2020, when the business expanded into a new state-of-the-art facility alongside its original location, bringing total manufacturing space to more than 40,000 square feet.

The company specializes in custom wire-wound electromagnetic products, including coil assemblies, transformers, encapsulated and toroidal assemblies, fine-wire assemblies, inductors and chokes, cable and connector harnesses, and electro-mechanical assemblies. Its vertically integrated operation covers manual and multi-spindle CNC winding (#4–#56 AWG), automated selective soldering, precision injection over-molding, vacuum pressure impregnation, epoxy and silicone encapsulation, selective conformal coating, and in-house 3D printing and tooling. Testing capabilities include HI-POT up to 20 kV, inductance, capacitance, resistance, impedance, turns ratio, and statistical process control. Annual output reaches millions of components, from prototype to full-scale production.

Able Coil serves aerospace and defense (avionics, satellite communications, radar), commercial and industrial, telecommunications, laser, medical (including imaging equipment), and music and audio markets. Customers range from OEMs requiring mission-critical reliability to commercial programs needing high-volume consistency.

The company differentiates itself through vertical integration that controls design, winding, assembly, and testing under one roof; collaborative engineering support with 3D modeling and rapid prototyping; flexible manufacturing from single units to millions; and a commitment to tight tolerances, complex geometries, and stringent environmental requirements without compromise.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC multi-spindle winding", "Manual winding", "Automated selective soldering", "Precision injection over-molding", "Vacuum pressure impregnation (VPI)", "Epoxy encapsulation", "Silicone encapsulation", "Selective conformal coating", "3D modeling and drafting", "Rapid prototyping and 3D printing", "In-house tool design and machining", "Collaborative engineering design support", "Transformer manufacturing (dry, impregnated, VPI, encapsulated)", "Electrical testing (inductance, capacitance, resistance, impedance, HI-POT to 20 kV, turns ratio, surge stress)", "Statistical process control (SPC)", "Coil winding (random, wet, bondable, precision, orthocyclic, universal)", "Wire processing (#4\u2013#56 AWG, various insulations, shapes, materials)"], "industries": ["Aerospace & Defense", "Commercial & Industrial", "Telecommunications", "Laser", "Medical", "Medical Imaging", "Music & Audio"], "materials": ["Copper", "Aluminum", "Litz wire", "Cupron", "Nichrome", "Other alloys", "Wire insulation per NEMA MW 1000 (Class B, F, H)", "Ceramic", "Steel", "Aluminum", "Brass", "Magnetic alloys", "Torlon", "PEEK", "Ultem", "Delrin/Acetal/POM", "Rynite/PET", "Ryton/PPS", "Zytel/Nylon", "LCP", "DAP", "Teflon/PTFE", "G10", "Phenolic", "GPO3", "Epoxy", "Silicone"], "equipment": ["CNC Winding Systems", "Multi-spindle CNC winding machines", "Automated Selective Soldering machines", "Shuttle and rotary table injection molding machines", "3D printers (additive manufacturing)", "In-house machine shop"], "volume": "Prototype to millions of units annually", "lead