UPDATE companies SET description='The business was founded in 2001 by Joshua Decker and Ben Moses, starting with a single shift knob imported from Germany and sold online. Decker, who began his German-car journey with a 1986 VW Jetta GLI, expanded the catalog to include turbos and complete RS4 body kits before selling the company in 2006 to Bill Spencer, owner of Hartmann Wheels, a brand that has supplied the U.S. market since 1978. Spencer, a three-decade veteran of German-car tuning, now owns and directs Achtuning.

The company specializes in the distribution and installation of performance parts for Audi, Volkswagen, BMW, and Porsche vehicles. As an authorized distributor for brands including APR, Centric Parts, Girodisc, H&R, Hartmann Wheels, and StopTech, Achtuning stocks a high volume of inventory on site for immediate shipment or installation. The Redmond facility houses offices, a retail showroom, a main warehouse, and a seven-lift installation bay. A staff of ten, each of whom owns and works on German cars, handles everything from basic oil changes to brake service, scheduled maintenance, and full performance builds.

Achtuning serves the European car enthusiast community through its physical storefront and an international location in Korea. The company sponsors regional events and online forums such as Audizine, QuattroWorld, and VWVortex, and is a proud sponsor of Audi Club Northwest, the largest Audi enthusiast group in the Pacific Northwest.

The business distinguishes itself by maintaining deep stock levels — 40,000 square feet of storage by one account — and by testing parts on its own vehicles, both street and track, before offering them for sale. As an authorized distributor, Achtuning guarantees genuine products without knockoffs or factory “B-Stock,” backed by manufacturer technical support.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Performance parts distribution", "Parts installation (7 lift bays)", "Performance tuning", "Maintenance and repair services", "Wheel mounting and balancing", "Brake upgrade installation", "Authorized distribution for APR, Centric Parts, Girodisc, H&R, Hartmann Wheels, StopTech", "Inventory stocking and immediate shipment", "European vehicle specialization (Audi, VW, BMW, Porsche)"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "European car performance parts", "Audi, VW, BMW, Porsche enthusiast market"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["7 lift installation bay"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Largest stocking distributor for APR, Centric Parts, Girodisc, H&R, Hartmann Wheels, and StopTech", "27,000 sq ft facility with seven-lift installation bay and on-site inventory for same-day shipping", "Authorized distributor status ensuring genuine parts, no knockoffs or B-stock, with factory tech support", "Staff of ten, all German-car owners with hands-on experience", "Physical retail and installation location in Redmond, WA, plus an international store in Korea"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2001 by Joshua Decker and Ben Moses -> /about-us", "Sold to Bill Spencer in 2006 -> /about-us", "Currently owned by Bill Spencer of Hartmann Wheels -> /about-us", "Hartmann Wheels since 1978 -> /", "Facility: 27,000 sq ft Redmond WA with offices, showroom, warehouse, 7 lift installation bay -> /about-us", "40,000 sq ft storage mentioned -> /", "Staff of 10, all own German cars -> /about-us", "Authorized distributor for APR, Centric Parts, Girodisc, H&R, Hartmann Wheels, StopTech -> /about-us", "Largest stocking distributor of those brands -> /about-us", "Physical store front in Redmond, WA and international store in Korea -> /about-us", "Sponsors local shows and online forums (Audizine, QuattroWorld, VWVortex) and Audi Club Northwest -> /about-us", "Test parts on own cars street and track -> /about-us", "No knockoffs or B-stock -> /about-us", "Services: performance tuning, parts, service, maintenance, repair, installation -> /, /about-us", "Wheel mounting, brake upgrades -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Achtuning specializes in the distribution and installation of quality parts from APR, Centric Parts, Girodisc, H&R, Hartmann Wheels, and StopTech. We are the largest stocking distributor of these quality brands, keeping our inventory on site for immediate shipment or installation for the benefit of our customers, the European car community.", "founded_year": "2001", "employee_count": "10", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='achtuning' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='ACO, Inc. operates from a 90,000-square-foot facility in Oklahoma City, Oklahoma. The company was founded in 1972 by Jerry Asner and remains a family-owned business now in its third generation, led by President David Asner, CFO Esther Stephenson, and VP Operations Andrew Feiler.

The company specializes in custom plastic injection molding and tooling, running 20 molding machines that include proprietary structural foam equipment capable of producing parts up to six feet cubed or 250 pounds. ACO provides a full turnkey operation: free consultation, part design, prototyping, tooling built and maintained in its on-site tool and die shop, CNC machining, CAD drafting, secondary operations, assembly, finishing (engraving, hot stamping, metal forming, bending, sonic welding), and custom jigs and fixtures. It handles small to large batch production runs and stores tooling for the life of each project.

ACO serves customers across a broad range of industries, leveraging its ability to process a wide variety of engineering-grade materials including polyethylene (HDPE, LDPE), polypropylene, ABS, polycarbonate, PPS, nylon, PVC, and specialty alloys such as Static Intercept, Corrosion Intercept, Carmelstat, Noryl, Santoprene, Pelethane, and Durethane.

The company emphasizes its family-owned culture, low employee turnover, and Oklahoma work ethic as differentiators. It guarantees tooling storage for the life of a project, offers one-on-one communication, and aims for faster turnaround times through its integrated in-house workflow.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom plastic injection molding", "Tooling design and manufacturing", "Prototyping", "CNC machining", "CAD drafting", "Secondary operations", "Assembly", "Finishing (engraving, hot stamping, metal forming, bending, sonic welding)", "Custom jigs and fixtures", "Structural foam molding", "Turnkey manufacturing", "Project lifecycle management"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Polyethylene (High Density, Low Density)", "Polypropylene", "ABS", "Static Intercept", "Corrosion Intercept", "Carmelstat", "Noryl", "Polycarbonate", "PPS", "Santoprene", "PVC", "Nylon", "Pelethane", "Durethane", "Other engineering grade materials"], "equipment": ["20 injection molding machines", "Proprietary structural foam machines", "CNC machining equipment", "Tool & die shop equipment"], "volume": "Small or large batch production runs", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Guaranteed tooling storage for the life of the project", "Turnkey in-house operation from design through shipping", "Proprietary structural foam machines capable of 6-foot cube / 250 lb parts", "On-site tool & die shop with CAD drafting", "One-on-one communication and faster turnaround times"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1972 by Jerry Asner -> /about-us", "Family-owned, third generation -> /about-us, /", "90,000 sq ft facility in Oklahoma City -> /about-us, /", "20 injection molding machines -> /about-us, /", "Proprietary structural foam machines capable of 6-foot cube / 250 lb parts -> /about-us, /", "On-site tool & die shop -> /about-us, /", "Turnkey operation: design, develop, produce, store in one location -> /", "Materials: Polyethylene, Polypropylene, ABS, Static Int