UPDATE companies SET description='Acton Custom Enterprises, LLC operates from Holderness, New Hampshire, where it was founded in 2008 by Nick and Bonni Acton. Nick, a native of New Zealand with degrees in mechanical and production engineering, had spent a lifetime modifying and racing cars before a stint with Camp Counselors USA brought him to the Lakes Region. He met Bonni in 1993, and their shared automotive passion evolved from a hobby into a family-owned specialty shop. Bonni, a former corrections officer and school board member, manages the office and operates shop machinery, while their sons Vance and Carl assist with fabrication and sandblasting.

The company manufactures nearly 500 catalog parts across 29 categories and provides custom fabrication services from a facility equipped with a CNC plasma table, Bridgeport mill, lathe, hydraulic press, tube bender, English wheel, and welding equipment for TIG, MIG, stick, and aluminum. Core activities include scratch-building replica cars, restoring original Cobras, completing unfinished projects, and producing historically accurate components such as custom oil pans, cold-air boxes, and programmed dash panels. The shop also offers worldwide pre-purchase inspections, authentication of original Cobras, and on-site restoration travel.

Acton Custom serves the Cobra replica and classic-car restoration market, supplying parts to restoration experts and selling vehicles internationally. Customers range from individual enthusiasts seeking a custom-built replica to collectors requiring verification of originality. The business has shipped products and provided consulting services globally.

The founders emphasize old-world craftsmanship and exacting attention to detail, rooted in Nick’s engineering background and hands-on approach. The company differentiates itself by offering historically accurate details, custom solutions for tall drivers, and the ability to fabricate parts that do not yet exist, all produced in the United States.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Scratch build dream car", "Original car restoration", "Build replica car", "Completion of unfinished projects", "International buying and selling of cars", "Verification and authentication of original Cobras", "Pre-purchase inspections worldwide", "Consultation on originality and details", "Travel for restoration work worldwide", "Custom fabrication (custom height oil pan, cold air box)", "Historically accurate details and parts", "Custom build for tall drivers", "Custom programming dash panels", "Custom programming firewalls", "CNC plasma cutting", "Welding (TIG, MIG, Stick, Gas, Aluminum)", "Brake/Shear operations", "Bridgeport milling", "Lathe work", "Hydraulic pressing", "Tube bending", "Tube rolling", "Blasting", "English wheeling", "Shrinking/stretching"], "industries": ["Cobra restoration", "Custom automotive fabrication", "Classic car restoration", "Replica car manufacturing", "Automotive parts manufacturing"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["CNC Plasma Cutting Table (up to 3/8\")", "Welder & Spool Gun (TIG, MIG, Stick, Gas, Aluminum)", "Brake/Shear", "Bridgeport", "Lathe", "Hydraulic Press", "Tube Bender", "Tube Roller", "Blasting", "English Wheel", "Shrinker/Stretcher"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Old-world craftsmanship and exacting attention to detail", "Nick\u2019s engineering background and lifetime hands-on experience", "Historically accurate details and parts for Cobra and custom cars", "Custom fabrication of non-existent parts (e.g., custom height oil pan, cold air box)", "Worldwide pre-purchase inspections and on-site restoration travel", "All parts made in the U.S.A."], "facts_used": ["Founded 2008 -> db", "Headquarters Holderness, NH -> db", "Family-owned -> /about", "Small business -> /about", "Nick mechanical engineering background -> /about", "Bonni office admin and machine operation -> /about", "Nearly 500 products across 29 categories -> /capabilities", "Manufacturing capabilities in-house -> /capabilities", "Equipment list -> /capabilities", "Services list -> /capabilities", "Supplied parts to Cobra restoration experts -> /about", "Worldwide pre-purchase inspections -> /capabilities", "Custom fabrication examples -> /capabilities", "Historically accurate details -> /about", "Made in USA -> /capabilities"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Acton Custom has its own manufacturing capabilities, meaning if it doesn''t exist yet, it will. Everything is made right here in the U.S.A.", "founded_year": "2008", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='acton-custom-enterprises-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Adaptive Technologies Inc. (ATI) was founded in 2001 in Nampa, Idaho, and operates as an owner-operated plastic injection molding company. The business is backed by the owner’s decades of hands-on experience in part functionality, moldability, and patent considerations.

ATI provides in-house part design, CAD modeling, and prototyping services alongside mold design and plastic injection molding. The facility runs nine injection molding machines with clamp tonnage ranging from 85 to 500 tons and shot capacity up to 72 ounces, supporting projects from first articles through full production runs. A fully equipped quality department verifies parts against detailed written and visual instructions.

The company serves a broad range of industries including construction, electronics, food and beverage, firearms, sports and outdoors, agricultural, medical, consumer, transportation, and automotive.

