UPDATE companies SET description='Advanced Underground Utility Locating Inc. was founded in 2002 in Bend, Oregon. The company operates offices throughout Oregon and Washington and is licensed to serve California and Idaho.

The firm specializes in private and public utility locating, offering complete utility detection and mapping, advanced utility locating, electrical fault locating, water leak detection, ground penetrating radar scanning, and floor or interior concrete scanning. Technicians use GPS data collection to produce high‑resolution utility maps exportable in KML, KMZ, SHP, and PDF formats, and they also employ drone photogrammetry for geo‑locked aerial imagery.

Services are aimed at residential, commercial, and industrial clients, including homeowners planning small digs, contractors managing large‑scale construction, and facility managers overseeing complex underground infrastructure. The company notes that its mapping helps avoid costly replanning and damage during excavation.

AUUL differentiates itself with the claim “If We Can’t Find It… It Can’t Be Found,” emphasizing its ability to locate utilities that other providers miss through the latest GPR technology and comprehensive mapping that includes depth, pipe size, and material identification.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Complete Utility Detection and Mapping", "Advanced Utility Locating", "Electrical Fault Locating", "Water Leak Detection", "Ground Penetrating Radar (GPR) Scanning", "Floor/Interior Concrete Scanning", "GPS Utility Data Collection", "Reference Mapping", "Drone Satellite Photogrammetry"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Homeowner"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Ground Penetrating Radar (GPR) systems", "Drone photogrammetry platform"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["GPS coordinates integrated into utility markings and high\u2011resolution maps", "Drone satellite photogrammetry for geo\u2011locked aerial site imagery", "Latest Ground Penetrating Radar technology to detect utilities others miss", "No job too big or too small, with technicians across Oregon, Washington, California, and Idaho", "Maps exportable in KML, KMZ, SHP, and PDF formats"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2002 -> db", "Headquarters Bend, Oregon -> db", "Offices throughout Oregon and Washington, licensed in California and Idaho -> page ''/''", "Completed 61,943 projects -> page ''/''", "Services: Complete Utility Detection and Mapping, Advanced Utility Locating, Electrical Fault Locating, Water Leak Detection, Ground Penetrating Radar, Floor/Interior Scanning -> page ''/''", "GPS utility data collection, high-resolution maps, drone photogrammetry -> page ''/services''", "Reference mapping accuracy within 5ft -> page ''/services''", "Slogan: If We Can''t Find It... It Can''t Be Found -> page ''/''", "Serves residential, commercial, industrial, homeowner -> page ''/services''"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We provide underground utility locating services from Eugene down I-5 to Roseburg, OR.", "founded_year": "2002", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='advanced-underground-utility-locating' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='AdvancedPCB traces its roots to 1977 when Advanced Printed Circuit Technology (APCT) was founded in Santa Clara, California. The company now operates under the unified AdvancedPCB name following a 2024 merger of APCT, Advanced Circuits, and San Diego PCB Design. Its headquarters are in Aurora, Colorado, with additional manufacturing and engineering sites in Santa Clara, Chandler, Anaheim, Maple Grove, and Orange County.

The company provides end-to-end printed circuit board solutions, including design services, fabrication, and assembly. Its fabrication capabilities span quick-turn prototypes, standard multilayer boards (up to 10 layers), advanced high-density interconnect (HDI) and ultra-HDI designs (up to 40 layers), flex and rigid-flex circuits (1–6 layer flex, 4–22 layer rigid-flex), RF/microwave boards, and heavy-copper constructions. Assembly services cover turnkey, kitted, and partial fulfillment with lead, RoHS, and no-clean solder options, and no minimum volume requirements. Turnaround times range from same-day to four weeks, with manufacturing turns as fast as 24 hours.

AdvancedPCB serves aerospace and defense, telecommunications and networking, medical technologies, industrial and robotics, and data center, networking, and storage markets. Its boards meet IPC Class 2 and Class 3 standards, and the company holds AS9100 quality certification for aerospace programs. Customers include engineers and product teams developing everything from satellite systems and medical devices to cloud infrastructure and robotic controls.

The company emphasizes domestic manufacturing as a differentiator, operating multiple U.S. facilities to protect intellectual property, ensure ITAR compliance, and enable faster collaboration. It also offers a hybrid model with vetted offshore partners for non-ITAR, high-volume production. Free design-for-manufacturability (DFM) checks, proprietary design software (PCB Artist), and a “strive to say yes” service philosophy round out its value proposition.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ITAR','AS9100','CMMC']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB design services (DFM review, impedance calculation, panel utilization, array drawings)", "PCB fabrication: quick-turn prototypes", "PCB fabrication: standard multilayer (0-10 layers, FR-4)", "PCB fabrication: advanced HDI and UHDI (up to 40 layers)", "PCB fabrication: flex circuits (1-6 layers)", "PCB fabrication: rigid-flex circuits (4-22 layers, up to 4X HDI lamination cycles)", "PCB fabrication: RF/microwave boards", "PCB fabrication: heavy copper multilayer", "PCB fabrication: custom materials", "PCB assembly: turnkey, kitted, partial fulfillment", "PCB assembly: lead, RoHS, no-clean solder", "Free DFM file check", "PCB Artist design software", "Trace width calculator", "Vendor-managed inventory (VMI)", "Global offshore manufacturing (non-ITAR)", "Strip-etch-strip line"], "industries": ["Aerospace & Defense", "Telecommunications & Networks", "Medical Technologies", "Industrial & Robotics", "Data Centers, Networking & Storage"], "materials": ["FR-4", "RF materials", "Aluminum clad", "Custom materials"], "equipment": ["Strip-Etch-Strip Line"], "volume": "1 - 1000+ units (standard PCBs); no minimum volume (assembly)", "lead_time": "As fast as 24 hours; same-day to 4 weeks depending on complexity", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Manufacturing turn times as fast as 24 hours", "No minimum volume on assembly orders", "Free DFM file checks and proprietary design software (PCB Artist)", "ITAR-compliant data submission and U.S.-based manufacturing", "Vendor-managed inventory (VMI) programs and seamless recipe transfer for offshore production"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1977 as APCT in Santa Clara -> /about-us", "Headquarters Aurora, Colorado -> /about-us", "Multiple U.S. facilities (Santa Clara, Chandler, Anaheim, Maple Grove, Orange County) -> /about-us", "ISO 9001:2015 certified, ITAR registered -> db, /quality", "AS9100 quality certification for aerospace -> /", "CMMC certification achieved -> /", "Fabrication: quick-turn prototypes, standard multilayer up to 10 layers, HDI/UHDI up to 40 layers, flex 1-6 layers, rigid-flex 4-22 layers, RF/microwave, heavy copper, custom materials -> /", "Assembly: turnkey/kitted/partial, lead/RoHS/no-clean solder, no minimum volume -> /", "Turnaround: as fast as 24 hours, same-day to 4 weeks -> /", "Industries served: aerospace/defense, telecom/networking, medical, industrial/robotics, data centers -> /", "Free DFM checks, PCB Artist software, trace width calculator -> /", "Vendor-managed inventory, offshore manufacturing for non-ITAR -> /", "Strip-etch-strip line investment -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "American-Based Manufacturer of Cutting-Edge Printed Circuit Boards for Every Industry", "founded_year": "1977", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "No minimum volume", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='advancedpcb-aurora-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='AeroParts Manufacturing & Repair, Inc. operates a 128,000-square-foot facility in Rio Rancho, New Mexico. The company has been providing aircraft component repair and manufacturing services for over 50 years.

As a build-to-print manufacturer, AeroParts produces complex sheet metal components using drop-hammer forming, supported by an in-house foundry, heat-treatment, and welding operations that hold NADCAP and AS9100 accreditation. The company also repairs metal and composite parts such as ducts, plenums, and mufflers, and specializes in restoring ozone converters through its proprietary AeroCLEAN® and AeroCOAT® processes. Additional capabilities include repair of nitrogen generation system components, along with testing and inspection services. AeroParts maintains FAA, EASA, and CAAC repair station certifications and employs over 100 technicians and tradespeople.

The company serves the commercial aviation sector, with a customer base that includes major airlines such as Aero-Mexico, Air France, Alaska Airlines, American Airlines, Asiana Airlines, Boeing, British Airways, China Airlines, Delta TechOps, Hawaiian Airlines, Korean Airlines, Lufthansa, Singapore Airlines, Southwest Airlines, United Airlines, and UPS.

AeroParts emphasizes reducing customer downtime and replacement costs through faster turnaround and lower-cost solutions, a philosophy it calls High Performance. Its proprietary ozone converter restoration processes have a proven track record of more than two decades, extending service life and lowering operating costs. The company also highlights innovative repairs for nitrogen generation system components, offering improved reliability and fast turn times.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100 Rev D','NADCAP Heat Treatment','NADCAP Weld','FAA Repair Station License','EASA Repair Station License','CAAC Maintenance Organization Certificate','ANAC Argentina','CAA UK','CAAV']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Build-to-print sheet metal manufacturing", "Drop-hammer metal forming", "In-house foundry", "Heat treatment (NADCAP accredited)", "Welding (NADCAP accredited)", "Ozone converter repair (AeroCLEAN\u00ae process)", "Ozone converter repair (AeroCOAT\u00ae process)", "Nitrogen generation system component repair", "Metal and composite component repair", "Testing and inspection", "Custom ductwork manufacturing"], "industries": ["Commercial aviation", "Aerospace", "Airline MRO"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary AeroCLEAN\u00ae and AeroCOAT\u00ae processes for ozone converter restoration", "In-house foundry, heat treatment, and welding with NADCAP accreditation", "Drop-hammer metal forming for complex sheet metal components", "FAA, EASA, and CAAC repair station certifications", "Build-to-print manufacturing of complex sheet metal components"], "facts_used": ["Facility size 128,000 sq ft -> /about-us", "Over 100 employees -> /about-us", "Over 50 years in business -> /about-us", "Build-to-print manufacturer of complex sheet metal components -> /", "Drop-hammer metal forming capabilities -> /", "In-house foundry, heat treatment, welding NADCAP and ISO/AS9100 accredited -> /", "Proprietary AeroCLEAN\u00