inary repeatability, remarkable responsiveness -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "manufacturing custom-designed electromagnetics at the highest levels of quality and value", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='agile-magnetics-a-standex-electronics-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Alabama Steel Supply operates from Montgomery, Alabama, where it was founded in 1912 by Romanian immigrant Jacob Labovitz as a scrap metal, fur, and paper business. Four generations later, the company remains family-run under President Barry Labovitz on the same West Boulevard site.

The firm manufactures metal roofing and siding panels (26 and 29 gauge), pre-engineered buildings, pole barn kits, barndominium packages, carports, and structural steel components such as purlins, girts, trusses, plate, tubing, and surplus pipe. Production runs on the company''s own roll-forming lines with in-house engineering, allowing panels to be cut to exact job dimensions and trim fabricated to match. The plant ships to all 50 states; pole barn packages typically leave in about two weeks, while pre-engineered buildings average 10–12 weeks.

Customers include contractors, farmers, facility managers, and homeowners across construction, agriculture, commercial, and residential sectors. The company also works with distributors and suppliers regionally. Projects range from clear-span warehouses and equipment covers to single sheets of roofing sold over the counter.

Alabama Steel Supply differentiates itself by controlling the full chain—rolling, engineering, and fabricating in-house rather than brokering third-party panels. The same sales representative handles quoting, project management, and post-delivery support, and the company emphasizes straight answers even when a lower-cost option fits better.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Roll-forming (metal roofing/siding panels)", "In-house engineering (stamped, code-ready plans)", "Metal fabrication (trim, structural components)", "Cut-to-length panel processing", "Pre-engineered building design and manufacturing", "Pole barn kit manufacturing", "Barndominium package manufacturing", "Carport and cover manufacturing", "Structural steel fabrication (purlins, girts, trusses, plate, tubing, pipe)", "Factory-applied protective coatings", "Nationwide shipping", "Counter pickup", "Project management", "Sales consulting (code, load, lead time advice)"], "industries": ["Construction", "Agriculture", "Commercial", "Residential"], "materials": ["26 gauge steel", "29 gauge steel", "Galvanized steel", "Structural steel (purlins, girts, trusses, plate, tubing, pipe)"], "equipment": ["Roll-forming lines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Pole barn packages ~2 weeks; pre-engineered buildings 10\u201312 weeks", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Manufacturer, not a middleman: rolls own panels on in-house roll-forming lines", "In-house engineering produces stamped, code-ready plans", "Panels cut to exact job dimensions, not catalog SKUs", "Same sales rep before, during, and after the sale", "Support after delivery: install questions answered by the same team"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1912 by Jacob Labovitz -> /about-us", "Family-owned, four generations -> /about-us", "Headquarters Montgomery, AL -> /about-us", "Manufactures metal roofing, siding, pre-engineered buildings, pole barns, barndominiums, carports, structural steel components -> /", "Own roll-forming lines and in-house engineering -> /", "Panels cut to exact dimensions -> /", "26 and 29 gauge steel with long-life coatings -> /", "Ships to 50 states -> /", "Lead times: pole barns ~2 weeks, pre-engineered buildings 10-12 weeks -> /", "Customers: contractors, farmers, facility managers, homeowners -> /", "Same sales rep before, during, after sale -> /", "Support after delivery -> /", "Barry Labovitz President -> /about-us", "Location 2 West Blvd, Montgomery, AL 36108 -> /about-us", "Founded year 1912 -> db", "Headquarters city Montgomery -> db", "Headquarters state Alabama -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "A manufacturer, not a middleman. We roll them ourselves \u2014 which is why our quality, our lead times and our answers are all first-hand.", "founded_year": "1912", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='alabama-steel-supply' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Alamance Foods, Inc. is headquartered in Burlington, North Carolina. The company traces its roots to 1890 when R.W. Scott began selling butter and cream, and Alamance Foods was formally established in 1959 after becoming a co-manufacturer for a major aerosol whipped cream brand. It operates as a veteran-owned, family-led business.

It operates three manufacturing facilities in Burlington and Graham, North Carolina, with over 1,000 employees. Capabilities span custom formulation, flavor exploration, product development, food science, pilot plant testing, large-scale production, packaging, and logistics, with an annual capacity of tens of millions of cases.

Alamance Foods serves foodservice operators, consumer packaged goods companies, retailers, convenience retailers, and restaurant brands. Its own brand portfolio includes Classic Cream®, Coffee Toppers®, Fun Pops®, Fun Pops Drinks®, Groovy Glacier®, Whipt®, and Triton Water®. The company also provides co-packing and end-to-end private label solutions.

