es, injection molding power cords -> pages /", "Serves USA and Canada -> pages /", "Made in USA OEM Capabilities -> db capabilities and pages /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "American Cable Assemblies, is a privately-owned, US-based manufacturer of both standard and custom, high-quality fiber optic cabling, copper assemblies, & power cords.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='american-cable-assemblies' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='American HomePatient operates from Dover, Delaware, providing respiratory and home medical equipment services across the United States. The company has served patients for over 25 years, specializing in ventilator, oxygen, and sleep therapy equipment for home-based care.

The company supplies a range of durable medical equipment including ventilators, CPAP machines, oxygen systems, nebulizers, and enteral nutrition products. Through affiliated entities, it also offers pharmacy services dispensing FDA-approved pharmaceuticals, home INR testing, and wound care supplies. Services include disease management programs, clinical support, and caregiver education tailored to physician prescriptions.

American HomePatient serves patients with chronic respiratory conditions, obstructive sleep apnea, and mobility limitations in home settings. Its customer base includes ventilator-dependent individuals, those requiring long-term oxygen therapy, and tube-fed patients needing nutritional support.

The company emphasizes clinical support and customized therapy programs over simple equipment delivery, aiming to improve health-related quality of life for homebound patients. Its affiliated pharmacy network and in-home testing services extend care beyond standard DME provision, with programs designed to give patients as much normalcy as possible in their daily lives.', certifications=ARRAY['FDA-APPROVED']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Ventilator therapy equipment and support", "Oxygen therapy supplies and training", "Sleep therapy (CPAP) equipment and support", "Durable medical equipment (DME) provision", "Enteral therapy and nutrition support", "Home INR testing and PT/INR monitoring", "Nebulizer therapy equipment", "Pharmacy services (FDA-approved pharmaceuticals)", "Wound care supplies and support", "Disease management programs", "Caregiver education and clinical support"], "industries": ["Durable Medical Equipment (DME)", "Respiratory therapy", "Sleep therapy", "Home healthcare", "Enteral nutrition", "Wound care"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Ventilators", "CPAP machines", "Oxygen concentrators and supplies", "Nebulizers", "Enteral feeding pumps"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Clinical support and caregiver education for ventilator-dependent patients", "Customized therapy programs tailored to individual prescriptions", "Affiliated pharmacy network serving cities across America", "In-home INR testing and PT/INR monitoring through affiliate mdINR", "Over 25 years of experience in sleep therapy and CPAP technology"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Dover, Delaware -> db", "Specializes in ventilator equipment and aids -> /", "Offers oxygen therapy supplies, training, and education -> /", "Provides sleep therapy/CPAP for over 25 years -> /", "Supplies durable medical equipment for mobility -> /", "Affiliated pharmacy provides FDA-approved pharmaceuticals -> /", "Offers enteral therapy, home INR testing, nebulizer therapy, wound care, disease management -> /", "Staffed with healthcare professionals and clinicians -> /", "Customizes therapy programs to individual needs and prescriptions -> /", "Certification: FDA-APPROVED -> db", "Services offered through affiliated entities -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "American HomePatient\u00ae specializes in the provision of ventilator equipment and aids. We help patients maintain mobility in the home with a variety of Durable Medical Equipment. Our affiliated pharmacy serves cities and hometowns across America, providing FDA-approved pharmaceuticals.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='american-homepatient' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='American Leather Operations, LLC was founded by engineers in 1990 in Dallas, Texas, on the conviction that a twelve-week wait for custom furniture was too long. What began as a small team in a borrowed facility has grown into a privately held manufacturer employing more than 700 people in a 350,000-square-foot factory in Dallas.

The company handcrafts made-to-order residential and contract furniture, including sleeper sofas, motion sofas, recliners, stationary pieces, and accent chairs. Its Dallas facility produces frames from sustainably harvested wood, offers over 500 leather and fabric upholstery options, and uses water-based pigments and fire-retardant-free foams and fabrics. All leather scraps are recycled or resold, and the operation is a founding member of the Sustainable Furniture Council.

American Leather sells through more than 700 retail partners across the United States and supplies contract-approved collections for commercial and hospitality projects.

