UPDATE companies SET description='Amtech is a family-owned contract electronics manufacturer based in Troy, Michigan, founded in 1998. The company operates from a facility and has served OEMs, hardware startups, and venture-backed companies for more than three decades as a build-to-print partner, meaning customers retain design ownership while Amtech manufactures to exact specifications.

The company provides end-to-end electronics manufacturing services including PCB assembly (turnkey SMT and through-hole from prototype to mid-volume production), box build and mechanical assembly, custom wire harnesses with 100% electrical testing, functional and in-circuit testing, and product development support such as DFM/DFA. Production runs on AmtechOS, a proprietary ERP system, and the business operates on the Entrepreneurial Operating System (EOS). The firm emphasizes high-mix, low-volume programs alongside high-volume production, supported by advanced automation and in-house robotics platforms.

Amtech serves automotive (aftermarket, OEM Tier 2 ceramic substrate programs), industrial automation (20+ year partnerships), IoT, health and safety (mission-critical scale-ups), and defense/UAS supply chains with NDAA-compliant manufacturing. Customer testimonials cite long-term relationships dating to 1998 across automotive, industrial automation, and IoT sectors, with case studies highlighting 8-week program launches, custom PCB design with fixturing, and decade-long ceramic substrate soldering partnerships.

The company positions itself as a technology partner rather than a pure contract manufacturer, offering engagement models from tech facilitator to ODM-style support to production partner, all within a single framework that allows customers to expand services without changing partners, processes, or systems. Its 3R Promise — Reliable, Robust, and Responsive — underpins proactive communication and domestic manufacturing backed by a global supply chain.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 13485','NDAA-compliant manufacturing']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB Assembly (SMT and through-hole)", "Box Build & Mechanical Assembly", "Wire Harness Assembly", "Functional Testing", "In-Circuit Testing", "Product Development Support (DFM/DFA)", "Low-Pressure Overmolding", "Component Risk Analysis", "AVL Development and Alternate Sourcing", "Supply Chain Strategy and Lifecycle Planning", "On/Re-Shoring Support", "Custom Automation and Fixturing", "Counterfeit Prevention Policy (Authorized Channels Only)"], "industries": ["Automotive (Aftermarket, OEM Tier 2)", "Industrial Automation", "Internet of Things (IoT)", "Health & Safety / Medical", "Defense / UAS"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["AmtechOS (proprietary ERP)", "In-house robotics platforms"], "volume": "Prototype to mid-volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned, build-to-print model with customer design ownership", "Proprietary AmtechOS ERP for end-to-end program visibility", "Single-framework engagement models (Tech Facilitator, ODM-Style, Production Partner) allowing service expansion without partner change", "NDAA-compliant manufacturing for defense and UAS supply chains", "In-house robotics platforms and low-cost automation for global cost competitiveness"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1998 -> db, / (testimonial ''since 1998'')", "Family-owned, Troy, Michigan -> /about", "Build-to-print contract electronics manufacturer -> /about", "Facility at 701 Minnesota Drive, Troy, M