UPDATE companies SET description='Arizona Capacitors Inc. operates from Tucson, Arizona, where it was founded in 1951 under the name West-Cap. The company became a subsidiary of Electro Technik in 2010, joining a portfolio of passive electronic component businesses. Its facility is located

The firm designs and manufactures standard and custom wound film capacitors, including metalized plastic capacitors for industrial use. Custom capabilities include capacitor assemblies with wire harnessing for military vehicles, recessed pass-through capacitors, multi-channel input capacitor/filters, shock-mounted isolated pass-through capacitors, and high-power multi-channel capacitors. Many designs date to the 1950s, and the company cites over 70 years of continuous service.

Arizona Capacitors serves defense, aerospace, medical, telecommunications, grid, power conversion, industrial, and instrumentation markets. The company''s ETI Companies matrix shows its film capacitors, magnetics, filters, resistors, and RF/microwave products crossing these sectors. Concrete examples include military vehicle capacitor assemblies, military 4-channel input capacitor/filters, and high-power 4-channel capacitors.

The company emphasizes its long heritage and ongoing development of new products for future applications. It highlights its MIL-STD certification and CAGE code 0TCV9 as indicators of military compliance, and its integration within Electro Technik''s three business units—capacitive/resistive, microwave/RF, and magnetics/transformer products—as a source of expanded capability.', certifications=ARRAY['MIL-STD']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom wound film capacitor design and manufacturing", "Metalized plastic capacitor production", "EMI/RFI filter manufacturing", "Precision resistor manufacturing (wirewound, current sense, high temperature, high voltage, ultra-precision, SMD)", "RF/microwave component manufacturing (terminations, resistors, attenuators, circulators, isolators)", "Magnetics design and manufacturing (standard and custom transformers, MIL-STD-1553, MIL-PRF-27, space)", "Custom capacitor assembly with wire harnessing", "Recessed pass-through capacitor fabrication", "Multi-channel input capacitor/filter design", "Shock-mounted/isolated capacitor packaging", "Custom mechanical design integration", "High-power multi-channel capacitor manufacturing"], "industries": ["Defense", "Aerospace", "Medical", "Telecommunications", "Grid", "Power", "Power Conversion", "Industrial", "Instrumentation"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 70 years of continuous service with designs dating to the 1950s", "MIL-STD certification and CAGE code 0TCV9 for military compliance", "Custom wound film capacitor design and manufacturing for industrial and military applications", "Part of Electro Technik group with capacitive/resistive, microwave/RF, and magnetics/transformer business units", "Custom assembly capabilities including wire harnessing, shock mounting, and custom mechanical integration"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1951 as West-Cap -> db", "Acquired by Electro Technik in 2010 -> /", "Headquartered 