UPDATE companies SET description='Aurora Energy, Inc. is a commercial solar energy company based in Columbia, Maryland, founded in 1994. The firm serves businesses across Maryland, Washington, D.C., and Virginia, providing custom-designed, installed, and maintained solar power systems. No founder names or ownership details are disclosed.

The company manages the full project lifecycle: due diligence, engineering and design, permitting, installation, and ongoing operations. Aurora does not manufacture panels or perform residential installations.

Clients span commercial property management, government facilities, hospitality, agriculture, and non-profit sectors. Notable projects include the United Therapeutics Unisphere in Silver Spring — described as the world’s largest net-zero building — multiple hotel rooftops in the D.C. area, the first solar installation at the Pentagon, and systems for Bernstein Management Corporation, Meinhardt Properties, Shapiro & Duncan, Porter Construction, MOMI, Retired Racehorse Project, and Waredaca Farms.

