UPDATE companies SET description='Aurora Specialty Textiles Group operates from Yorkville, Illinois, where it has manufactured textiles in the United States for over a century. The company celebrated its 140th anniversary of domestic production in 2023. It functions as a subsidiary of Meridian Industries, Inc., a family-owned diversified manufacturing group founded in 1943 and based in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, which comprises five operating companies.

The company specializes in textile coating and finishing, offering a broad range of processes including coating, dyeing, fabric preparation, calendering, angle inducing, and converting services such as precision slitting to widths between 0.75 and 126 inches. Its dedicated research and development team supports new product innovation from concept through commercialization, and the firm also provides fabric sourcing for both woven and nonwoven materials from domestic and international suppliers. Quality control is conducted in on-site laboratories with in-line coat weight monitoring and a contamination-controlled rewind area.

Aurora serves markets that require pressure-sensitive tape backings, technical textiles, and printable textiles, engineering custom fabrics for diversified end-use applications. Its customer base includes businesses seeking coated and finished textile solutions across various industrial sectors.

The company emphasizes its commitment to quality and sustainability, holding ISO 9001 and ISO 14001 certifications. Its stated mission is to exceed customer expectations while providing a safe, collaborative workplace, and its vision targets North American leadership in textile finishing and coating through continuous investment in technology and skilled personnel.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 14001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Coating & Finishing", "Dyeing", "Fabric Preparation", "Calendering", "Converting Services", "Fabric Sourcing", "Angle Inducing", "New Product Innovation"], "industries": ["Pressure-sensitive tape", "Technical textiles", "Printable textiles"], "materials": ["Water-based textile coating compounds", "Woven fabrics", "Nonwoven fabrics"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 9001 and ISO 14001 certified quality and environmental management systems", "Precision slitting capability from 0.75\" to 126\" wide", "In-house R&D staff with proven product development track record", "In-line coat weight monitoring on coating lines", "Contamination-free, environmentally controlled final rewind area"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Yorkville, Illinois -> db", "140th anniversary of U.S. textile manufacturing celebrated in 2023 -> /", "Subsidiary of Meridian Industries, Inc., a family-owned group founded in 1943 -> /about", "ISO 9001 certified -> /quality", "ISO 14001 EMS certified -> db, /", "Processes: coating, finishing, dyeing, fabric preparation, calendering, converting, fabric sourcing, angle inducing, new product innovation -> /capabilities", "Converting: precision slitting 0.75\" to 126\" -> /capabilities", "Markets: pressure-sensitive tape backing, technical textiles, printable textiles -> /", "In-line coat weight monitoring, contamination-controlled rewind area -> /quality", "Mission and vision statements -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evi