UPDATE companies SET description='Automotive Parts Headquarters Inc. (APH) is a third-generation, family-owned aftermarket auto parts distributor headquartered in St. Cloud, Minnesota. The company traces its roots to 1920 when National Bushing & Parts Company incorporated in Minneapolis. Jack Bartlett joined the firm in 1938, became a financial partner in 1959, and with partners established APH in 1965. Leadership passed to his son John Bartlett in 1976 and to the third generation, Corey Bartlett, who became president in 2008.

Today APH operates three modern distribution centers, including a 160,000-square-foot facility expanded by 40,000 square feet in 2018, and supports a network of nearly 300 corporate and independent Auto Value parts stores across Minnesota, Wisconsin, North Dakota, South Dakota, Michigan, Montana, Iowa, Nebraska, and Wyoming. The company employs approximately 1,800 people and serves as a regional hub for the Aftermarket Auto Parts Alliance, which connects more than 2,200 parts stores and 3,000 certified service centers throughout North America.

APH’s customer base includes independent auto parts retailers, professional repair shops, and heavy-duty truck service providers through its affiliation with HDA Truck Pride.

The company says its differentiation lies in a service-first culture — “Service is the difference” — backed by core values of integrity, continuous improvement, and community support. APH highlights its family ownership and long-term relationships with suppliers and store owners as key to its ability to say “yes” to customer requests and maintain consistent parts availability.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Aftermarket auto parts distribution", "Warehouse and distribution center operations", "Retail auto parts store operations (Auto Value)", "Supply chain management for independent retailers", "Heavy-duty truck parts distribution (HDA Truck Pride)"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "Auto parts retail", "Automotive service and repair", "Heavy-duty truck parts"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated for three generations", "Network of nearly 300 Auto Value parts stores across nine states", "1,800 service-driven employees", "Member of the Aftermarket Auto Parts Alliance and HDA Truck Pride"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1920 as National Bushing & Parts Company -> /about", "Headquarters in St. Cloud, Minnesota -> /about", "Third-generation family-owned (Bartlett family) -> /about", "1,800 employees -> /about", "Three modern distribution centers, 160,000 sq. ft. facility expanded by 40,000 sq. ft. -> /about", "Nearly 300 Auto Value stores across nine states -> /about", "Member of Aftermarket Auto Parts Alliance -> /about", "Affiliated with HDA Truck Pride -> /about", "Core values and service-first culture -> /about", "Community involvement (WACOSA, American Cancer Society, etc.) -> /about", "Partnership with Bickle family (Warehouse Inc.) -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Automotive Parts Headquarters Inc. (APH) is a third-generation family-owned aftermarket auto parts distributor based in Sain