UPDATE companies SET description='Automotive Technology, Inc. (ATI) began in December 1982 and incorporated in 1983 in Fenton, Missouri. The company started with two employees working from a home office before moving into its own 10,500-square-foot facility.

ATI operates as a full-line distributor and service provider for the automotive and collision repair industry. The company sells and installs equipment from manufacturers such as Hunter Engineering (alignment systems, wheel balancers, tire changers), Global Finishing Solutions (paint booths), Rotary (lifts), Chief (frame racks and measuring), Prospot (welding), and Graco (lubrication). Its service department handles paint booth installation and maintenance, lift installation and repair (both in-ground and above-ground), diagnostic equipment service, on-site brake lathe repair, frame rack and welder service, and wheel balancer and tire changer service. ATI is also an authorized repair center for Robinair, Accuturn, and Corgi equipment.

The company serves mechanical repair shops and collision repair facilities throughout the St. Louis metropolitan area, including Chesterfield, Clayton, Florissant, Kirkwood, University City, and Ballwin. Its customer base consists of independent repair shops and body shops requiring equipment sales, installation, and ongoing maintenance.

ATI traces its differentiation to early market adoption; it was one of the first distributors to bring downdraft paint booths to the U.S. in the 1980s, initially importing Saico booths from Italy. The company emphasizes a commitment to follow-through, encapsulated in its stated principle: "We complete what we start, and we do what we say."', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Paint booth installation and service", "Lift installation and service (in-ground and above ground)", "Diagnostic equipment service (automotive and collision repair)", "On-site brake lathe repair", "Frame rack and welder service", "Authorized repair center for Robinair, Accuturn, Corgi", "Wheel balancer and tire changer service", "Facility design and outfitting for collision repair shops"], "industries": ["Automotive repair", "Collision repair", "Mechanical repair", "Auto body"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Hunter HawkEye Elite alignment system", "Cool-Tech 34288 A/C machine", "Hunter wheel service products", "Global Finishing Solutions paint booths", "Rotary lifts", "Chief frame racks and measuring systems", "Prospot welding equipment", "Graco lubrication equipment", "Robinair recovery/recycling equipment", "Accuturn brake lathes", "Corgi equipment", "Spies Hecker automotive paint", "Nason automotive paint", "JBI industrial/aircraft paint booths", "Saico paint booths"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["One of the first distributors to introduce downdraft paint booths in the 1980s", "Authorized repair center for Robinair, Accuturn, and Corgi equipment", "Over 30 years of experience selling and servicing paint booths", "Helped design and outfit dozens of new collision repair facilities", "Complete sales and service for automotive and collision repair equipment"], "facts_used": ["Founded December 1982, incorporated 1983 -> /about", "Started with 2 employees working from home -> /about", "Current facility 10,500 sq ft in Fenton, MO -> /about", "Current headcount over 20 -> /about", "Primary objective: complete sales and service company for automotive and collision repair industry -> /about", "Early distributor of downdraft paint booths (Saico from Italy) in 1980s -> /", "Added Global Finishing Solutions paint booths in 2006 -> /about", "Sells Hunter Engineering alignment systems, wheel balancers, tire changers -> /about", "Sells Rotary lifts, Chief frame racks, Prospot welders, Graco lubrication -> /about", "Services: paint booth install/service, lift install/service, diagnostic equipment service, brake lathe repair, frame rack/welder service, wheel balancer/tire changer service -> /about", "Authorized repair center for Robinair, Accuturn, Corgi -> /about", "Serves St. Louis area including Chesterfield, Clayton, Florissant, Kirkwood, University City, Ballwin -> /about", "Company principle: ''We complete what we start, and we do what we say'' -> /about"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We were one of the first distributors to introduce Downdraft paint booths to the market in the 1980''s.", "founded_year": "1983", "employee_count": "over 20", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='automotive-technology' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Aviva Wholesale Inc. was founded in 2000 in Metairie, Louisiana, as a family-run and operated business. The company began by distributing and manufacturing textile goods, leveraging a network of over ten production plants located both domestically and internationally.

Today, Aviva operates as both a manufacturer and wholesaler, supplying a broad range of blank apparel — including T-shirts, hoodies, sweatshirts, and raglan shirts — alongside heat press machines, heat transfer vinyl (HTV), and vinyl cutting plotters. The company sources from overseas factories in countries such as Pakistan, China, India, Bangladesh, Turkey, and Egypt, maintaining direct relationships that allow for product development and control over manufacturing. Its product lineup features brands like Gildan, Bella+Canvas, Laviva Sports, LAT Apparel, Next Level, Silhouette, and Mimaki.

The primary customers are custom apparel businesses, screen printers, and heat-transfer decorators who purchase at wholesale or retail levels.

